 "text": "**Digest 2026-10-13 UTC** · #cd-tracker (dev, 222 tickets) · since 2026-10-13\n\n**Summary**\n• AUD-34 (AB-02) done: Bayesys reproduced (16 of 31 published PC-Stable/FCI cells within tolerance at alpha 0.05; PC 10 of 15). Bayesys's half-credit scoring moves at most 0.03 when columns are shuffled, so its table is not inflated by its layout; CausalArena's forced-choice tie-break is what rewards the leak. causal-learn GES shows an engine order effect on PROPERTY (-0.07 to -0.09).\n• DEC-06 / TEAM-08: Atlas v2 approved and built on the same GitHub Pages site: Home plus 11 pages in four acts (problem, findings, what we build, where we are) and a glossary, evidence index and about page. The build fails on terms used before they are taught, results shown before their question, missing numbers, broken links and unlabelled market figures.\n• DEC-05: reliability before features recorded for the wedge (ledger invariants, never below data-only, bounded harm, held-out calibration before any product).\n• EXT-01: the case for shuffled columns or tie-break-invariant scoring now rests on two benchmarks.\n\n**Done** (3)\n• ✅ AUD-34 AB-02 Second scoreboard: layout and conflict channels on other public benchmarks\n• ✅ DEC-06 Approve the Atlas v2 page sequence (and whether the market page is public)\n• ✅ TEAM-08 Atlas v2: the site as a guided sequence of pages (four acts, thirteen pages)\n\n**Due in the next 14 days**\n• 2026-10-16 CRS-07 Decision gate G1\n• 2026-10-19 CRS-01 TA check-in 1 (TA: Nate)\n• 2026-10-20 AUD-37 AB-05 LIVE (small): agent probes, install and one-run cost per agent ($5 cap)\n• 2026-10-20 BND-03 Paper and code audit: headline claims, methods text, untouched modules…\n• 2026-10-22 BND-02 Primary sources: literature re-reads, deep reads, method choices\n• 2026-10-24 BND-06 Remaining baselines, order sensitivity, scoreboard package (no LLM)\n• 2026-10-24 BND-08 LIVE: Causal-Copilot on CausalArena's named scenarios (old bundle 2)\n\nTotals: ✅ 110 · 👀 21 · ⏳ 